                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "527ec1aa-2714-3e91-87d0-3fb59ef809d8",
                        "entry_id": "86252303-e970-3847-8b2f-f5a4b26c98a5",
                        "glosses": [
                            "to stab (to death), to knife, to kill, to carve up; to butcher, to stick"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "a2eb8006-379b-4bf5-abed-dba7ae48b8cb",
                                "sense_id": "527ec1aa-2714-3e91-87d0-3fb59ef809d8",
                                "text": "Мне то́тчас рассказа́ли, что капита́на нашли́ с перере́занным го́рлом, на ла́вке, оде́того, и что заре́зали его́, вероя́тно, мертве́цки пья́ного, так что он и не услы́шал, а кро́ви из него́ вы́шло «как из быка́»[...]",
                                "translation": "I was told at once that the captain had been found with his throat cut, on the bench, dressed, and that he had probably been dead drunk when he was killed, so that he had not even felt it, and that he had bled \"like a bull\"…",
                                "english": "I was told at once that the captain had been found with his throat cut, on the bench, dressed, and that he had probably been dead drunk when he was killed, so that he had not even felt it, and that he had bled \"like a bull\"…"
                            }
                        ]
